I doubt it... One thing to check : I have found that MILO does some name=20
mangling when there are more than one period in the filename. For=20
example, even though the initrd's filename on the 2005.0 Gentoo LiveCD=20
is gentoo_2.4.igz, I have to type 'initrd=3Dgentoo_2_4.igz' in my boot=20
command. Maybe something similar is happening to you? At the MILO=20
prompt, try doing an 'ls' on your boot partition / directory to see what=20
MILO sees the filenames as.

Other than that, I don't have any other ideas... Generally, if you use=20
the filename as seen in an 'ls' from the MILO prompt, the kernel should=20
start to load, and after that it all depends on the build options and=20
other parameters in the boot command. With my MILO image, anyways, I can=20
boot my latest kernels without any problems.

Good luck,

J-S

